# compact = information-dense, assumes expertise
# balanced = mixed experience levels
# spacious = clarity over density, new or casual users
# This is the coarse label. The DENSITY taste dial below is the fine control —
# keep the two consistent (compact≈8-10, balanced≈4-7, spacious≈1-3).
density-profile:

## Taste dials
# Three 1-10 dials the skill chain calibrates every visual decision against.
# Set once here; commands like "bolder"/"quieter" nudge them per-task.
# Dials tune choices WITHIN the design system's guardrails — they never relax a
# safety, accessibility, or hard token rule (motion caps, reduced-motion,
# contrast, touch targets all still apply at every dial value).
#
# VARIANCE (1-10): layout asymmetry / willingness to break the grid.
#   1-3 = strict symmetric grids   4-7 = deliberate asymmetry   8-10 = editorial/masonry
# MOTION (1-10): animation richness (always inside the <300/500ms caps).
#   1-3 = near-static, essential feedback only   4-7 = fluid CSS transitions   8-10 = choreographed
# DENSITY (1-10): information per screen (numeric form of density-profile above).
#   1-3 = spacious/gallery   4-7 = balanced   8-10 = compact/cockpit
variance:
motion:
density:

